sub:assertion {
<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/levin-2014-tumor-07> a <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/Claim>;
    dc:description "Treating Xenopus laevis embryos with antibiotics that target gram-positive bacteria — novobiocin alone, or a cocktail of gentamicin, metronidazole, vancomycin and clindamycin — significantly increases the incidence of oncogene-induced tumor-like structures, implying that native butyrate-producing bacteria normally restrain tumorigenesis.";
    dc:type "experimental-result";
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Antibiotics against gram-positive bacteria increase tumor incidence";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/context> "Chernet BT, Levin M, “Transmembrane voltage potential of somatic cells controls oncogene-mediated tumorigenesis at long-range”, Oncotarget (2014), doi:10.18632/oncotarget.1935; section “RESULTS › Changes in Vmem”. Scope: Oncogene-injected Xenopus laevis embryos exposed to antibiotics in the rearing medium"
}
